<p>And I know I can hide out the overflowing items by using <code>overflow:hidden;</code> property but it is not always a good case.</p>
<p>For example, I tried to create a hamburger icon but I could not because of this overflow issue. The menu lines were working as if the entire element is shown but I had to hide it out so that it could fit into the header.</p>
<p>Here is the code -</p>
<pre><code>    &lt;header&gt;
  &lt;div class=&quot;logo&quot;&gt;
Elvis
  &lt;/div&gt;

   &lt;div class=&quot;menu&quot;&gt;
Hamburger Menu
  &lt;/div&gt;

&lt;/header&gt;
</code></pre>
<p>In CSS -</p>
<pre><code>    *{
