            }
            document.getElementById(&quot;demo&quot;).innerHTML = text;
          }
          &lt;/script&gt;
</code></pre>,"<p>The reason the first quantity is being accessed is because having multiple elements with the same <code>id</code> is invalid HTML - and typically browsers will return the first element in the document matching an <code>id</code> value supplied to <code>document.getElementById</code>.</p>

