Exception in thread "main" java.lang.IndexOutOfBoundsException: Source does not fit in dest<p>I have Object:</p>
<pre><code>static class Truck {

    ArrayList&lt;Integer&gt; route = new ArrayList&lt;Integer&gt;();
    double weight = 0;
    int route_weight = 0;

    Truck() {
    }

    Truck(ArrayList&lt;Integer&gt; route) {
        Collections.copy(this.route, route);
    }

    //getters and setters
}
</code></pre>
<p>Objects pulling into this list:</p>
<pre><code>static ArrayList&lt;Truck&gt; trucks=new ArrayList&lt;Trucks&gt;();
</code></pre>
<p>I'm trying to make a full copy of the list:</p>
<pre><code>        ArrayList&lt;Truck&gt; copy=new ArrayList&lt;&gt;();
        copy=cloneList(trucks);
</code></pre>
<pre><code>    public static ArrayList&lt;Truck&gt; cloneList(ArrayList&lt;Truck&gt; trucksList) {
        ArrayList&lt;Truck&gt; clonedList = new ArrayList&lt;Truck&gt;();
        for (Truck truck : trucks) {
            Truck w=new Truck(truck.getroute());
            clonedList.add(w);
        }
        return clonedList;
    }
</code></pre>
<p>But I'm getting a error:</p>
<pre><code>Exception in thread &quot;main&quot; java.lang.IndexOutOfBoundsException: Source does not fit in dest
</code></pre>
<p>getroute returns:</p>
<pre><code>[0, 9, 11, 1, 15, 3, 0]
</code></pre>,"<p><code>Collections.copy</code> requires that the size of the destination list is at least the size of the source list. Your <code>this.route</code> has a size of 0 when you try to do the copy so you get an exception.</p>

