}
</code></pre>
<p>For the first definition it is roughly <code>O(N²)</code> and for the second one <code>O(N)</code>.</p>,"<p>It would be <code>O(n)</code>. You are explicitly freeing up the memory after the assignment is done. I agree the inner workings of the <code>malloc</code> would be useful but assuming a normal implementation which doesn't use memory enough to change the space complexity ( For tracking <code>O(n)</code> memory allocation it keeps <code>O(n^2)</code> amounts of metadata - just a weird example).</p>

