<p>If the ul class stock has three items in the list, the space isn't huge, but if there's only two it's huge.</p>
<p>I've been trying to experiment with margins and it's still got quite a large gap in between if there's two rows.</p>
<p>How could I fix the margin so that if there's just two items in a list it's not a huge gap, currently I've been trying to fix gap, columns etc.?</p>,"<p>This is due to your <a href=""https://css-tricks.com/snippets/css/a-guide-to-flexbox/#aa-justify-content"" rel=""nofollow noreferrer"">flex justification</a> being <code>space-between</code>, which distributes an even amount of space between items. This is why two listings results in a larger gap than three.</p>

