<p>Ask 1 - Once the dot reaches finishing point B, I hope to be able to re-randomise x, y1, and y2 for my component.</p>
<p>Ask 2 - I need to have several instances of this component (say 20), each of which has their own random thing going on independently.</p>
<p><strong>My approach so far:</strong></p>
<p>Step 1: In the component's css file, I write the animation code with <code>--x</code>, <code>--y1</code>, and <code>--y2</code> as variables in the <code>:root</code> class:</p>
<pre><code>:root {                 /* Values assigned are just fallback values */
  --x: 100px;
  --y1: 10px;
  --y2: 400px;
}

.spark div {            /* spark is the `className` for the div that contains the dot (shown in Step 2) */
