How to change the CSS bundle name using a Webpack config override in CRA?<p>I currently have a <code>config-overrides.js</code> file that I use to change the bundle names that Create React App generates for JS files. I'd love to be able to apply similar logic to my CSS bundles.</p>
<p>Here are the contents of the config overrides files:</p>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>module.exports = function override(config, webpackEnv) {
  const isEnvDevelopment = webpackEnv === 'development';
  const isEnvProduction = webpackEnv === 'production';

  config.output.filename = isEnvProduction
    ? 'static/js/[name].js?nocache=[contenthash:8]'
    : isEnvDevelopment &amp;&amp; 'static/js/bundle.js';
  config.output.chunkFilename = isEnvProduction
    ? 'static/js/[name].chunk.js?nocache=[contenthash:8]'
    : isEnvDevelopment &amp;&amp; 'static/js/[name].chunk.js';

  return config
}
</code></pre>
<p>How can I achieve the same results but for CSS bundles/chunks?</p>
