    navbar.classList.add(&quot;sticky&quot;)
  } else {
    navbar.classList.remove(&quot;sticky&quot;);
  }
}

  &lt;/script&gt;
&lt;/body&gt;
&lt;/html&gt;`
</code></pre>,"<p>You need to place each image, text, and button, all in the same parent element, then place the parents in a flexbox. This will group them all together and cause them to layout together.</p>

Smoothly Animating Image Position and Scale to Fit the Screen in HTML/CSS<p>I want to animate an image when clicked to fill the whole screen, in such a way that seamlessly transitions from its original position to its full size, and back again, <a href="https://medium.com/javascript-in-plain-english/introduction-to-the-html-dialog-element-39a369d80028" rel="nofollow noreferrer">like on Medium.</a></p>
