trigger tooltip on button based on search field value<p>I want to show a tooltip on the button as long as the search field is empty.</p>
<p>what I have tried:</p>
<pre><code>// hover feature
const searchBtn = document.querySelector('.find__btn');

searchBtn.addEventListener('mouseover', () =&gt; {
  const searchText = document.querySelector('.find__field');
  console.log(searchText.value);
  if (searchText.value.length === 0) {
    jQuery(searchBtn).tipso({
      titleContent: 'Hello',
    });
  }
});
</code></pre>
<p>the problem with this implementation is it works only the first time. I mean, if I write something in the search field and hover over the button the tooltip is not visible and that is what I want. but the problem is If I make the search field empty and hover over the button, the tooltip is not visible.</p>
<p>so, it works only the first time. how can I fix it?</p>,"<p>You can initialize your <code>tipso</code> plugin on page load. Then , you can simply use <code>tipso('show')</code> or <code>tipso('hide')</code> depending on the condition to hide/show tooltip .</p>

